From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cinders of Chaos <noreply@cindersofchaos.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Minimap: bitmap window around the view centre on wide floors

MapMinimapService::rebuild() makes one Indexed8 bitmap of the whole floor,
cut at 8192 x 8192 tiles from the smallest x and y of the floor. Our floor 7
holds the base world near x 32000 and hunt areas near x 14400 (areagen_config.lua
origins), a span of about 20000 tiles. The bitmap started at x 14400 and ended
at 22591: the world the owner looks at was outside it, MinimapView::paint drew
only the dark background and the white view rectangle (owner screenshot, O586).

The bitmap is now a window of at most 8192 tiles around the focus tile, the
tile the minimap is centred on (the view centre; the town / preview centre
tile). It is rebuilt when the focus gets within 512 tiles of a side that has
more map behind it, or leaves it. A floor that fits keeps the old bitmap and
never rebuilds. A tile edited outside the window but inside the floor is
skipped instead of invalidating the bitmap.
